    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent 8 years building something that actually mattered, and it just... evaporated. it feels like there's this fundamental law of entropy at work in my life. every project, every attempt to build something stable just results in total systemic collapse. it's not even bad luck anymore, it feels like a mathematical certainty. like, if you look at the trajectory of my last few years, the math just points to zero. there's no way to optimize out of this kind of decay.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
